body:
After `create_action()`, you can iterate over adding methods for each point, and they are merged with the final `commit_action()` like:

```cpp
ur->create_action(TTR("Some oparation for points"));
ur->add_do_method(c.ptr(), "set_point_in", 0, Vector3());
ur->add_undo_method(c.ptr(), "set_point_in", 0, c->get_point_in(0));
ur->add_do_method(c.ptr(), "set_point_in", 1, Vector3());
ur->add_undo_method(c.ptr(), "set_point_in", 1, c->get_point_in(1));
ur->commit_action(); // Make only 1 action.
```

FYI, if you don't want to merge, there is an optional argument for `create_action()` as `UndoRedo::MergeMode`.

